! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F206C "TEST UNCHANGED
! REGISTERS" for ADD MAGNITUDE TO MEMORY (docs/jb_af1c_floating-
! point.pdf p.85, octal 014244.40-014274.40): two sub-tests that
! M+MG, whose result goes to STORAGE, leaves both accumulator halves
! and the sign byte exactly as it found them.
!   C1 "zeros remain zeros": C0000 clears both accumulator halves and
!     CM0000 the sign byte, ROS := FPK37, M+MG(U),ROS, then the left
!     half (CT0101 at offset 64, C1A), the right half (CT0101 at
!     offset 0, C1B) and all eight sign-byte bits (CT0011 at 10.0,
!     C1C) must still be zero.
!   C2 "ones remain ones": the same with C1111 / CM1111 against FPK1,
!     checked with the complement functions CT1010 and CT1100.
! Both use the accumulator only as the source of a magnitude, so
! nothing about it may change -- the to-memory mirror of F205C, where
! the accumulator was the destination and it was the RIGHT half and
! the sign byte's spare bits that had to survive.
!
! Substitutions (SSIP framework, real listed addresses): SERS (octal
! 1304) -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch, ROS (octal 22355)
! the memory operand, PASS -> the routine's exit at 014274.40 (the
! listing's "BD,$+1.0", followed by B,SAP7D / SIC,SEN0+.32 / B,SSW).
! Constants from the pool p.176.
!
! Instructions: BD, B, L(BU)/ST(BU), C0000/C1111 (connect to
! accumulator) with offset 64, CM0000/CM1111 (connect to memory) on
! the sign byte at 10.0, M+MG(U), CT0101/CT0011/CT1010/CT1100, SIC,
! BRGZ. verify_fp_arith_f206c_listing.py checks every word bit-for-bit.
!
! Observed: passes on the model as it stood after F206A/F206B. M+MG
! never writes the accumulator, so nothing here could have failed once
! the to-memory path stopped touching it -- this block is what says so
! rather than leaving it assumed.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0
        SLC, (8)22355.0
ROS     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pool p.176) --

        SLC, (8)22005.0
FPK0    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000000000000000000000
        SLC, (8)22006.0
FPK1    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777777777777777777777
        SLC, (8)22052.0
FPK37   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031125252525252525240

! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)14244.40
SAP7D   BD, $+.32   ! F206C1: zeros remain zeros
        L(BU), FPK37
        ST(BU), ROS
        C0000(BU,64), FPK0, 64
        C0000(BU,64), FPK0
        CM0000(BU,8), 10.0
        M+MG(U), ROS
        CT0101(BU,64), FPK0, 64   ! does L 0-63 remain
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0101(BU,64), FPK0   ! does R 0-63 remain
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0011(BU,8), 10.0   ! does the SB remain
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32   ! F206C2: ones remain ones
        L(BU), FPK37
        ST(BU), ROS
        C1111(BU,64), FPK1, 64
        C1111(BU,64), FPK1
        CM1111(BU,8), 10.0
        M+MG(U), ROS
        CT1010(BU,64), FPK1, 64   ! does L 0-63 remain
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT1010(BU,64), FPK1   ! does R 0-63 remain
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT1100(BU,8), 10.0   ! does the SB remain
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
PASS    BEW, $                  ! 014274.40: the routine's exit ("BD,$+1.0")
        END, SAP7D
